{"type":"message","id":"d0736391","parentId":"1c66bb31","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:04:15.616Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file was uploaded successfully. Now I need to get the file_token. The result doesn't explicitly show the file_token. Let me check what was returned and proceed to add a record to the bitable with the attachment. The file_token might be in the result or I might need to search for it.\n\nActually, looking at the result, it seems the upload succeeded but didn't return the file_token explicitly. Let me try to write a record with the attachment. For attachments in bitable, the format is typically `[{file_token: \"xxx\"}]`.\n\nLet me first try to create a record with the file. But I need the file_token. Let me see if I can list files or if the file_token was returned somehow.\n\nActually the feishu_drive_file upload result shows file_name and size but not file_token. Let me try to search for the file or use it in the record creation and see what happens.\n\nWait, actually for bitable attachments, I need to use the file_token. Let me try creating a record with the attachment field and see what format it expects. The file_token for attachments in bitable should be the drive file token.\n\nLet me just try creating the record and see if it works, or ask for the file_token.\n\nActually let me try the record creation and see what happens.","thinkingSignature":"f14f0768d7bd2b83800335d01fa97f8b29e82a845a5e45da3070c6d7ee6b6b93"},{"type":"text","text":"上传成功！现在写入记录附上图片 👇\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_oplj7kksew7i_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"create","app_token":"BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f","table_id":"tbl3oA2By4N3FTPh","fields":{"名称":"成都天气图","图片附件":[{"file_token":"demo_weather.png"}]}}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":11222,"output":395,"cacheRead":29582,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41199,"cost":{"input":0.0