{"type":"message","id":"19a92e87","parentId":"999769d1","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:09:15.034Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the record without the attachment field was created successfully. So the table and fields are working. The issue is with the attachment field value format.\n\nThe file_token returned from upload was \"demo_weather.png\" which is the original filename, not a real Feishu file token. That might be why it's failing - the attachment field probably expects a real file token, not just a filename.\n\nLet me update that record to add the attachment. But first I need to figure out the correct format. Let me try with just a simple test - maybe the file_token from upload isn't a real token. Let me check if there's a way to get the actual file token from the upload response.\n\nActually wait - the upload response was:\n```\n{\"success\":true,\"file_token\":\"demo_weather.png\",\"file_name\":\"demo_weather.png\",\"size\":52567}\n```\n\nThis looks like it just returned the original filename as the token. This might be a limitation - perhaps the upload didn't actually upload to Feishu but just returned the local filename? Or maybe it's a bug in the drive tool.\n \nThe upload did return success though, so let me try the record update with the attachment using that file_token to see what happens.","thinkingSignature":"620dfb95df401992493546b1d116ed73d672856a398eb80baf0a501bf0a4ad80"},{"type":"text","text":"写入成功了！问题是 file_token 格式——上传返回的是原文件名，不是飞书真正的 token 😅\n\n让我更新这条记录试试：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8kze4kvhosya_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"update","app_token":"BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f","table_id":"tbl3oA2By4N3FTPh","fields":{"图片附件":[{"file_token":"demo_weather.png"}]},"record_id":"recveVO3e6Ka1L"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":13406,"output":402,"cacheRead":29582,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43390,"