{"type":"message","id":"69a42934","parentId":"1dec3fd9","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:09:44.187Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still asking for authorization. It seems the batch_auth doesn't fully work for all permissions - there might be a mismatch between what the batch auth can grant vs what individual API calls request.\n\nThe user said \"授予所有用户权限，一次性搞定\" - they want to grant all permissions in one go. But batch_auth already says all 20 are granted. The issue is that the feishu plugin might be requesting new/different scopes that aren't in the batch auth.\n\nLet me think... The batch_auth tool said \"您已授权所有可用权限（共 20 个），无需重复授权。\" - this means the batch auth has already granted 20 scopes. \n\nBut individual API calls still fail saying they need authorization for base:record:update. There seems to be a disconnect. Either the batch auth isn't properly persisting the authorization state, or the API is requesting a scope that wasn't included in the original batch. Maybe I should try calling batch_auth again since it just re-sent the card - perhaps the user needs to interact with it again to fully authorize all the new scopes being requested.\n\nActually, I already got an \"auth-complete\" message earlier, so the issue might be that I misunderstood what that message meant. Let me try a different approach: I'll use batch_auth with the force_refresh parameter to ensure I'm getting the most current authorization state rather than relying on cached results.","thinkingSignature":"4b5c3ad01c61094f8621c704eb54eb68335bffc5143c93d74c01e393d823bf26"},{"type":"text","text":"批量授权显示20个权限都有了，但API还在要授权...可能是状态没同步。再发一次强制刷新：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_o2zfeelzdrak_1","name":"feishu_oauth_batch_auth","arguments":{}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":14095,"output":322,"cacheRead":29582,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43999,"cost":{"input":0.0042285,"output":0.00038639999999999996,