{"type":"message","id":"75b134d0","parentId":"8835c6d6","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:24:05.513Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user completed the auth again. Let me try the workaround - using the doc_media upload to insert the image into a doc and get a proper file_token. Or let me try to directly invoke the Feishu API using curl to see what the actual response looks like, and then figure out the correct token format.\n\nActually, let me try to fix the issue from a different angle. The user sent an image earlier (the DDR5 diagram). I should be able to download that image using the feishu_im_bot_image tool, but it failed with 400. Let me try the feishu_im_user_fetch_resource tool instead, since that works with the user's identity.\n \nWait, the bot image download failed - that's the bot's own download endpoint. Let me pivot and use the doc_media insert tool to upload the image directly into a Feishu doc, which should give me a usable file_token that I can then use to add it as an attachment to the bitable record.\n\nI already have the image locally, but I need the actual Feishu file token, not just the local path. The doc_media insert might work, though it's designed for documents rather than bitable attachments. Looking at what I have to work with - there's a demo weather PNG in /tmp, the image from the user's message, and the bitable setup with the app token, table, and record ID. Let me try the doc_media approach since it can insert images into documents.\n\nThe issue is that I don't have the document ID yet, and creating one requires going through the authorization flow again. The real problem is that the upload response isn't returning the file token properly. I could try working around this with the message image directly - when a user sends an image in Feishu, it gets a image_key and I could try using that key as the file_token for the attachment field, though I suspect it won't work since Feishu expects its own token format for bitable attachments.\n\nLooking back at what the user sent me, they forwarded an image from another chat with the file key img_10dc595d7fbdbe0698289af07a3797f5, but the bot image download failed with a 400 error. Let me reconsider the approach here.\n\nI think the real issue might be that I need to use the user's身份 to fetch the resource instead. Let me try calling feishu_im_user_fetch_resource with the message_id and file_key to get the image through the proper API.","thinkingSignature":"1b41b94b3f7bcb3b27f632a305a3f5b85cbe838f58ba8762d6c0cefd5c485fdc"},{"type":"text","text":"好，继续！让我换个思路——用户之前发过一张图片，我用用户身份下载下来再试：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bhhzt6p8a8ws_1","name":"feishu_im_user_fetch_resource","arguments":{"message_id":"om_x100b537c30bc48b0c1422ab78552226","file_key":"img_10dc595d7fbdbe0698289af07a3797f5","type":"image"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":142,"output":621,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":30466,"totalTokens":64541,"cost":{"input":0.0000426,"output":0.0007452,"cacheRead":0.00199872,"cacheWrite":0.011424750000000001,"total":0.014211270000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774488222031,"responseId":"0613bd9f89e0588741818f3b9df3f3aa"}}
