{"type":"message","id":"54c3cf31","parentId":"8999b874","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:24:30.357Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting auth errors. The issue is the `im:message:readonly`, `im:message.group_msg:get_as_user`, `im:message.p2p_msg:get_as_user` scopes aren't authorized despite batch_auth saying everything is granted.\n\nLet me think about a completely different approach. The user wants to upload an image to a bitable attachment field. The core problem is:\n\n1. `drive.file.uploadAll` returns `file_token` but the plugin code can't access it (bug)\n2. Various message reading scopes keep requiring auth\n\nWhat if instead of trying to fix the upload, I use the user's image that they sent in the chat? When a user sends an image in Feishu, the image is stored on Feishu's servers. The image_key in the message can be used directly in some contexts.\n \nI could try using the image_key from the user's message directly in the bitable attachment field - in Feishu, message image keys like `img_xxx` might actually work as file tokens for attachment fields since they're already on the server. Let me test this approach rather than continuing to fight with the upload API.","thinkingSignature":"33ae60b823cd04e76fa6c981017f42622936670dbb3a6f9aa36dac33226b3240"},{"type":"text","text":"等等，我发现一个关键问题——我一直在研究 plugin 的 upload 逻辑，但其实有更简单的绕路方法。\n\n**用户发给我的图片**，已经在飞书服务器上了，有 `image_key`。而 bitable 附件字段可能直接支持 `image_key`！\n\n让我直接试试把用户发过来的图片的 `image_key` 当作 token 写入附件字段：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_gsphxt6ob7ce_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"update","app_token":"BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f","table_id":"tbl3oA2By4N3FTPh","fields":{"图片附件":[{"file_token":"img_10dc595d7fbdbe0698289af07a3797f5"}]},"record_id":"recveVO3e6Ka1L"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":31514,"output":448,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65274,"cost":{"