{"type":"message","id":"4bd93c85","parentId":"1aac2e37","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:25:36.846Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Those are all node_modules files, not what I need. Let me look at the actual OpenClaw config to find the Lark plugin config.\n\nActually, instead of trying to trace through the config, let me take a completely different approach. Since the core problem is that `drive.file.uploadAll` returns a `file_token` but the plugin code doesn't return it properly, and given that I can't easily run a direct test...\n\nWait, I just realized something. Let me look at the actual return value from `feishu_drive_file` upload again. The result was:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"file_name\": \"demo_weather.png\",\n  \"size\": 52567\n}\n```\n\nNotice there's NO `file_token` at all. But the code clearly does:\n```javascript\nreturn json({\n    file_token: res.data?.file_token,\n    file_name: fileName,\n    size: fileSize,\n});\n```\n\nIf `res.data?.file_token` is `undefined`, it would show as `null` or be omitted in the JSON response. The fact that it's completely absent suggests either `res.data` is undefined or `res.data.file_token` doesn't exist in the actual API response.\n\nI think the issue might be with how the Feishu PHP SDK formats the response. Looking at the file structure, there are separate SDK files for different languages - `node-sdk` and `php-sdk`. The PHP SDK might be wrapping responses differently than expected, which could explain why `file_token` isn't making it through to the final output.\n\nRather than continuing to trace through the SDK code, let me check if there's a way to retrieve the uploaded file's metadata using the `get_meta` action - that might give me the `file_token` if I can get the file name or other identifying information. But I'd need to know the `file_token` for `get_meta` to work, so that's circular. \n\nThe most direct approach would be to call the Feishu API directly using curl with the access token, but I don't have the user token available. Instead, let me try a different action - maybe `doc_media` insert will work if I can locate a document to work with.","thinkingSignature":"129285894701c348148d06dd446fa8e010780f2081a1d7317e607fec0cd2cde6"},{"type":"text","text":"让我换个方向——试试用 `feishu_doc_media` 的 insert 接口，它可能用了不同的 upload API，能返回正确的 token：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0q3bz1fwr4g7_1","name":"feishu_create_doc","arguments":{"markdown":"测试","title":"测试文档-图片上传"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":34099,"output":525,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67936,"cost":{"input":0.0102297,"output":0.0006299999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00199872,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.012858419999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774488320739,"responseId":"0613be0218558c4dc1e049875426c8fe"}}
