{"type":"message","id":"255a074e","parentId":"3e62b128","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:26:33.984Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`AttachFieldConvFail` - this means the attachment field conversion failed. The format I used (`\"img_10dc595d7fbdbe0698289af07a3797f5\"` as a plain string) is not the right format for an attachment field.\n\nThe correct format for an attachment field in Feishu bitable is:\n```json\n[{\"file_token\": \"file_xxx\"}]\n```\n\nSo it needs to be an array of objects with `file_token` keys. But the issue is that `file_token` needs to be a valid Feishu drive file token, not an image key.\n\nOK let me think about this from scratch one more time:\n\nThe fundamental chain is:\n1. Upload file to Feishu drive → get `file_token` \n2. Use `file_token` in bitable attachment field → success\n\nStep 1 is failing because the plugin returns `{ file_name, size }` without `file_token`.\n \nMaybe I can work around this by creating a new record and attaching the image directly to it, rather than trying to upload first. When users add attachments through the bitable UI, there's likely a different API call being made that handles the upload and attachment in one step. Let me try creating a record with an attachment field and see if I can intercept that flow.\n\nActually, I think the real issue might be with how the bitable record API handles attachment fields. When updating an attachment field with a file token, the API expects a specific format that might be different from what I'm sending. Let me try the update call again with the proper array syntax for the attachment field.\n\nWait—I just realized the user already has the image in their chat with me. That's a message attachment, not a drive file, so it won't work as a file token. The image has to actually exist in Feishu Drive first before I can attach it to a record. And the upload API is giving back a `box_` prefix instead of what I need.\n\nLet me step back and think about what the user is really asking for. They want automatic image uploads to bitable. Maybe I'm overcomplicating this—what if there's a different API endpoint or approach I'm missing that handles both upload and attachment in one step, or at least gets me past this token format issue?","thinkingSignature":"9435dd22dabad2f02848431e2048bf02f5fb2a9fab3f7289327d33a1f6a31308"},{"type":"text","text":"`AttachFieldConvFail` 说明格式还是不对。让我试试一个完全不同的 approach——直接用 Python 写死一个 curl 来测试 Feishu API，看上传后到底返回什么：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_7sp0eqjocplg_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 先找一下 openclaw 的配置，看看 feishu app_id\nfind /Users/edy/.openclaw -name \"*.json\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" 2>/dev/null | xargs grep -l \"app_id\\|feishu\\|lark\" 2>/dev/null | head -5"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":36091,"output":606,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70009,"cost":{"input":0.0108273,"output":0.0007272,"cacheRead":0.00199872,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.013553220000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774488377030,"responseId":"0613be3bd2f38a0e89916b073823146a"}}
