{"type":"message","id":"059d029f","parentId":"6afaa878","timestamp":"2026-03-26T01:27:10.152Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the issue! Looking at the SDK code:\n\nThere are TWO different `uploadAll` methods:\n1. `drive.file.uploadAll` - uploads to `/open-apis/drive/v1/files/upload_all`\n2. `drive.media.uploadAll` - uploads to `/open-apis/drive/v1/medias/upload_all`\n\nThe plugin uses `sdk.drive.file.uploadAll` which is the file upload API.\n\nNow, the key line is: `return (res === null || res === void 0 ? void 0 : res.data) || null;`\n\nSo the SDK returns `res.data`. If the raw HTTP response has `{ data: { file_token: \"xxx\", ... } }`, then `res.data` would be `{ file_token: \"xxx\", ... \n\n}` and `res.data.file_token` would be the token.\n\nBut the plugin is getting `undefined` for `res.data?.file_token`. This means either `res.data` doesn't have `file_token`, or `res.data` itself is `undefined` or `null`.\n\nWait, but the SDK returns `(res === null || res === void 0 ? void 0 : res.data) || null`. So if `res` is the full HTTP response, `res.data` would be the body. If the Feishu API returns `{ code: 0, msg: \"ok\", data: { file_token: \"xxx\" } }`, then the SDK extracts just the `data` part and returns it.\n\nSo the real question is what the plugin is actually receiving back from the SDK call.","thinkingSignature":"92ae5b782fde87e665f3cb06d436f20a4a8c401f3015ed451e8cd6126d3bc136"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_byjiq33w3xyy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"handleInvokeErrorWithAutoAuth\\|assertLarkOk\" /Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/helpers.js 2>/dev/null | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":39933,"output":391,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":73636,"cost":{"input":0.0119799,"output":0.00046919999999999997,"cacheRead":0.00199872,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01444782}},"stopReason":"toolUse