{"type":"message","id":"446e9f24","parentId":"bccf61ff","timestamp":"2026-03-26T02:26:32.610Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so I can list records. Now let me think about a workaround. \n\nActually, there's one more thing I could try. The `feishu_doc_media` tool with `insert` action - when you insert an image into a doc, it uploads to doc storage. But maybe there's a way to use the bitable API directly if I can figure out the right format.\n\nWait - actually, let me look at the problem from a different angle. The user is sending me images. Those images arrive as `image_key` in the message. Could the bitable attachment field accept an `image_key` instead of a `file_token`?\n\nLet me try creating a new record with the image_key directly:","thinkingSignature":"c2c5bac3a73e849c0ad778e644356d358df1c5aa1aab10d33865ebb2a762cea3"},{"type":"text","text":"让我试试直接用用户发过来的图片的 `image_key` 作为 token 创建记录：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_20cnlge1b2qi_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"create","app_token":"BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f","table_id":"tbl3oA2By4N3FTPh","fields":{"名称":"MRCD内存图","图片附件":[{"file_token":"img_10dc595d7fbdbe0698289af07a3797f5"}]}}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":40585,"output":295,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":74192,"cost":{"input":0.012175499999999999,"output":0.000354,"cacheRead":0.00199872,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.014528219999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774491982400,"responseId":"0613cc4fc6dc211ead0dcc8f9449a014"}}
