{"type":"message","id":"d74b36d3","parentId":"4f6a4e07","timestamp":"2026-03-26T02:27:00.028Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"That didn't work either. The `image_key` is not a valid `file_token` for bitable attachments.\n\nOK let me think about this completely differently. The user says \"I want to use it now.\" \n\nWhat if instead of trying to upload a NEW image, I try to use an existing image that was ALREADY uploaded through some other means? Let me check if the user's message with the image... wait, actually - when a user sends an image in Feishu, the image is automatically stored in Feishu's servers and has both an `image_key` (for messages) and potentially a `file_token` (for drive).\n\nThe `img_xxx` format is an image key for messages. \n\nBut bitable attachments might use `file_xxx` tokens instead. I've confirmed that `img_xxx` keys don't work for attachments - only `file_xxx` tokens do. The bitable storage system requires files to be uploaded through its own API, not just any file token. So the fundamental issue is that the current plugin lacks a tool to upload files directly to bitable storage.\n\nBut wait - there's another angle I haven't explored yet. When users send images in messages, those images are already stored on Feishu's servers. The message API gives me an `image_key`, but I'm wondering if that same image is also accessible through the drive API using a `file_token`. Let me try to see if I can access the user's image using the `image_key` somehow.\n\nActually, thinking about this more carefully - Feishu probably treats images sent in messages and images in drive storage as separate systems. The `img_xxx` key from messages likely won't work as a `file_xxx` token in bitable attachments. I keep going down dead ends here.\n\nThe real issue is that I need a way to upload files specifically to bitable's attachment storage, and the plugin doesn't currently have a tool for that. The `feishu_doc_media` insert tool is for documents, not bitables. Unless I could somehow use the message image that's already on Feishu's servers - but messages and bitable attachments appear to be completely separate storage systems.\n\nI should be honest with the user: the plugin needs a dedicated bitable file upload tool to make this work properly.","thinkingSignature":"b5fa0c7b8d885cf78067d667284c2b3021caad3ec1d02f9654057c71b8e2d39f"},{"type":"text","text":"<final>\n试了好几种方法都行不通 😅\n\n**根本原因总结：**\n\n| 我能做的 | 问题 |\n|---------|------|\n| `drive.file.uploadAll` | 上传到**云盘**，不是 bitable 存储 |\n| 用 `image_key`（用户发的图） | bitable 不认 `img_xxx` 格式，只认 `file_xxx` |\n| 用云盘的 file_token | 报错 \"attachment does not belong to this bitable\" |\n\n**结论：插件缺一个关键功能**\n\n飞书有**两套文件存储**：\n- 云盘（drive）✅ 插件能上传\n- 多维表格附件存储 ❌ **插件没有对应的上传接口**\n\n多维表格附件必须用 `POST /open-apis/bitable/v1/apps/{app_token}/tables/{table_id}/records/{record_id}/fields/{field_id}/attachments` 这个专用接口上传，但插件没实现这个。\n\n---\n\n**你要现在就用的话，有两个选择：**\n\n1. **手动来** → 打开表格，点「图片附件」字段手动上传（你之前说不想这样）\n\n2. **等插件更新** → 给 OpenClaw 飞书插件提 Feature Request，让作者加上 bitable 专用上传功能\n\n你现在最想要哪个？😔\n</final>"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":40905,"output":739,"cacheRead":33312,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":74956,"cost":{"input":0.0122715,"output":0.0008868,"cacheRead":0.00199872,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01515702}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774491993957,"responseId":"0613cc5c63077428f6fd43c800255893"}}
