{"type":"message","id":"6e4bb0c4","parentId":"627323ec","timestamp":"2026-03-26T06:06:13.126Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The node token is different from the bitable app token. The bitable app token `BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f` might not be a wiki node, so it can't be retrieved with wiki node API.\n\nLet me think about this differently. Looking at the Feishu UI - when you upload an attachment to a bitable field, the upload happens as part of the record creation/update process. The Feishu web UI likely does something like:1. Create/update record\n2. Simultaneously upload the file and attach it to the record\n\nBut the API approach (as documented) is:\n1. Upload file separately → get file_token (with bitablePerm in extra)2. Create/update record with the file_token in the attachment field\n\n\nSo the key insight is that `extra.bitablePerm` determines where the file is stored, while `parent_node` just needs to be a valid node and the file gets linked to the bitable through the record update. For bitable specifically, I need to figure out what value to pass as `parent_node` - it might need to be the parent folder or space token rather than the bitable ID itself. So the file gets uploaded to the bitable's storage through the `extra.bitablePerm` parameter, while `parent_node` just needs to be a valid token even if empty. The real issue is that I'm getting a \"parent node not exist\" error, which suggests `parent_node` can't actually be blank - I need to provide a real node token, likely the bitable app token itself.\n\nLooking at the Feishu material system more carefully, each upload target (docx, sheet, bitable) has its own media storage tied to that document's permissions, so `parent_node` probably needs to reference that specific document.\n\nBut wait—the error \"parent node not exist\" suggests the node does exist but the media upload can't find it. For bitable specifically, the upload goes through the bitable permission system with `extra.bitablePerm`, so maybe `parent_node` should be empty or the bitable app token works as the parent reference.\n\nThe API docs say `parent_node` is always required for all types except `ccm_import_open`, so it's not about being optional—it's about what value it accepts. Let me try the bitable app token directly in the `parent_node` field to see if that resolves the lookup issue.","thinkingSignature":"8a41ce325ce90ba08120a04110cd8c2722d4b9fb6ef1fb8ee7b6a7c28469a0eb"},{"type":"text","text":"根据官方文档，bitable 的 `extra.bitablePerm` 需要包含 `tableId` 和 `attachments` 映射。但关键问题是 `parent_node` 填什么。\n\n让我直接看飞书 SDK 源码里 `media.uploadAll` 的 `parent_node` 参数定义：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9agq8luookar_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -A 30 \"bitable_image\\|bitable_file\\|parent_node.*string\\|parent_type.*bitable\" /Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/feishu/node_modules/@larksuiteoapi/node-sdk/types/index.d.ts 2>/dev/null | head -60"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":73496,"output":658,"cacheRead":33389,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":107543,"cost":{"input":0.0220488,"output":0.0007896,"cacheRead":0.0020033399999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02484174}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774505151215,"responseId":"0613ffc0932981e486f0b835271bc7e0"}}
