{"type":"message","id":"6d7ff5ae","parentId":"9407f0a6","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:22:59.535Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, but `drive.file.uploadAll` doesn't support `parent_type=bitable`. Looking at the file.js code, it hardcodes `parent_type: 'explorer'` for all cases. So I can't use `drive.file.uploadAll` with `parent_type=bitable`.\n\nLet me reconsider. The issue is that `drive.media.uploadAll` with `parent_type=bitable_image` and `parent_node=app_token` gives \"parent node not exist.\"\n\nWhat if for `bitable_image` uploads, the `parent_node` should actually be the **wiki node token** of the bitable, not the app_token?\n\n\nActually, I think the problem might be that `app_token` and `node_token` are different identifiers. I should try using the wiki node token instead, though I don't have direct access to it. Alternatively, maybe `drive.media.uploadAll` doesn't validate `parent_node` strictly and I should try passing an empty string like I did initially—though that gave \"parent node not exist,\" so perhaps the issue is elsewhere. Let me reconsider what `drive.file.uploadAll` actually supports for `parent_type` values.\n\nLooking at the API docs, it seems to only support specific types like `doc_image`, `docx_image`, `sheet_image`, and others, but not `bitable_image` or `bitable_file` directly. That would explain why passing `parent_type=bitable` to `drive.file.uploadAll` doesn't work either. Maybe the real problem is that I need to upload to a folder first, then update the bitable record with the file token afterward. Let me step back and reconsider this from the Feishu UI's perspective.\n\nActually, I should look at the Feishu API docs more carefully to understand how attachments work. The documentation says files need to be uploaded first to get a `file_token`, then that token is used when creating or updating records. So `drive.media.uploadAll` should be the right approach, but I need to figure out the correct `parent_node` value for bitable attachments. Maybe `bitable_image` has a special requirement I'm missing, or perhaps the node needs to be in a specific format. Let me try using the folder token instead and see if that resolves the issue.\n\nWait, I'm realizing the confusion—`drive.media.uploadAll` and `drive.file.uploadAll` are actually different APIs with different response formats. The `drive.file.uploadAll` returns `file_xxx` tokens meant for general Drive files, while `drive.media.uploadAll` returns `boxcnxxx` tokens specifically for media attachments. I was using the wrong API. Let me switch back to `drive.media.uploadAll` and try setting `parent_node` to an empty string to see what happens.","thinkingSignature":"57698826af00c2629ddb9bf243b621b8e2ed52e2e3020c1549a06a9319eea5e1"},{"type":"text","text":"等等，`drive.file.uploadAll` 和 `drive.media.uploadAll` 是不同的！`file` 返回 `file_xxx`，`media` 返回 `boxcnxxx`。我用错了。换回来，但这次仔细研究下正确的 `parent_node`：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rs5aj44o57pu_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js","old_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    // 尝试用 drive.file.uploadAll（parent_type=bitable），parent_node 用 app_token\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.file.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: 'bitable',\n            parent_node: p.app_token,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });","new_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    // 使用 drive.media.uploadAll，parent_node='' 让飞书自动处理\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: '',\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n            extra: JSON.stringify({\n                bitablePerm: {\n                    tableId: p.table_id,\n                },\n            }),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79814,"output":1051,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":33389,"totalTokens":114254,"cost":{"input":0.0239442,"output":0.0012611999999999999,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.012520875,"total":0.037726275000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774509116944,"responseId":"061411b5d42e11995887faaa598b0c9a"}}
