{"type":"message","id":"c30eb6d0","parentId":"f5740460","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:23:34.461Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK let me think about the `parent_node` problem. I've been getting \"parent node not exist.\" when using `parent_node=''`. And earlier I tried `parent_node=app_token` and also got \"parent node not exist.\"\n\nWhat if the `parent_node` for bitable media uploads needs to be the `node_id` of the bitable in the wiki/folder system, not the `app_token`?\n\nFor a bitable, there are multiple identifiers:\n1. `app_token` = `BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f` - the app-level token for API calls\n\n\n2. `node_token` = the wiki/node token for the bitable's location in the folder hierarchy\n\nThese might be different! I need to find the `node_token` for the bitable, which is what the drive API probably needs for `parent_node`. I could try getting it through the wiki node API, or maybe using `drive.v1.files.list` to find bitable nodes in the folder. Actually, I'm realizing the user's existing bitables like \"兮兮的错题本\" might already have attachments with proper `boxcnxxx` tokens that I could examine to understand the structure better.\n\nIf I list the records in one of those existing bitables, I might be able to see what `file_token` format is actually being used for their attachments. Let me try that approach instead.","thinkingSignature":"19a8fff9fd2c946e92b3007cd12ec16c25cca8bf2c7f16697bbe0e8092ab88b4"},{"type":"text","text":"让我换个方向——看看你之前已有的「兮兮的错题本」里的附件 token 长什么样，从这里反推正确的上传方式：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_t6vim58ipxhz_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"YoHJbARduagO2ls0uvpcG9XNnNg","table_id":"tblxxx","page_size":1}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":81818,"output":408,"cacheRead":33389,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":115615,"cost":{"input":0.0245454,"output":0.0004896,"cacheRead":0.0020033399999999997,"