{"type":"message","id":"4cfaf09e","parentId":"4d6b3ec5","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:26:48.596Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ugh, another authorization needed. Let me think about this differently.\n\nThe key problem is `parent_node` for `bitable_image`. Let me approach this with fresh eyes.\n\nLooking at the Feishu API documentation for `drive.media.uploadAll`:\n- For `docx_image`: `parent_node` = doc_id\n- For `bitable_image`: `parent_node` = ?\n\nThe docs say for `bitable_image`: \"The parent_node is used to specify the specific document or location to which the media will be uploaded.\"\n\nBut looking at the material overview document: \"For bitable_image/bitable_file: The extra field is used to specify the bitable permission (bitablePerm).\"This strongly suggests that `extra.bitablePerm` is what determines WHERE in bitable the file is stored. The `parent_node` might just need to be a valid node_id that the app has access to, and the actual bitable routing happens through `extra`.\n\n\nMaybe `parent_node` doesn't need to be the bitable itself—perhaps any valid node token works, like the folder containing the bitable. The bitable's folder token is `nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf`, but I haven't tried that approach yet since the folder isn't actually the parent_type for bitable uploads. Let me reconsider whether the real issue is something else entirely, like how the SDK structures the multipart form data when `parent_node` is included.\n\nActually, I'm wondering if `drive.media.uploadAll` even accepts `parent_node` as a form field for bitable types, or if there's a separate internal endpoint the Feishu web UI uses that I'm not aware of. Let me step back and look at the actual API docs for bitable attachment uploads to understand the proper flow instead of continuing to guess.\n\nThe documented approach is straightforward: first upload the media to get a file token, then create a bitable record and attach that token to the appropriate field. But there's a circular dependency here—the record needs a field ID to attach to, yet the field might be created dynamically. I'm thinking I should create a static field in the bitable first, then upload the media, then update the record with the token. The issue is that the bitable upload endpoint keeps returning \"parent node not exist,\" which suggests the parent reference is malformed or the node doesn't actually exist in the system.\n\nLet me reconsider the node structure. Maybe for bitable uploads, the parent node should be the folder token, not the app token. I have the folder token from the drive listing, so let me try constructing the request differently using the folder as the parent reference instead.","thinkingSignature":"1393d6fc41e9593826f640012593f5115fa6ed42420fefdccab57f8e5b199aa0"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_7l324sbl2089_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js","old_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    // 先尝试不带 extra，看 parent_node 到底填什么能过\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: p.app_token,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });","new_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    // 尝试用 folder token 作为 parent_node\n    const folderToken = 'nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, folder=${folderToken}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: folderToken,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":88485,"output":974,"cacheRead":33389,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":122848,"cost":{"input":0.0265455,"output":0.0011688,"cacheRead":0.0020033399999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02971764}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774509978815,"responseId":"0614129e5064b169f215f1c17219664c"}}
{"type":"message","id":"b707888f","parentId":"4cfaf09e","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:26:48.637Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_7l324sbl2089_1","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 377         });\n 378     }\n 379     const fileName = path.basename(filePath);\n 380     const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n-381     log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n-382     // 先尝试不带 extra，看 parent_node 到底填什么能过\n+381     // 尝试用 folder token 作为 parent_node\n+382     const folderToken = 'nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf';\n+383     log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, folder=${folderToken}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n 383     const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n 384         data: {\n 385             file_name: fileName,\n 386             parent_type: parentType,\n-387             parent_node: p.app_token,\n+388             parent_node: folderToken,\n 388             size: fileSize,\n 389             file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n 390         },\n 391     }, opts), { as: 'user' });\n     ...","firstChangedLine":381},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774510008628}}
{"type":"message","id":"6faea6e6","parentId":"b707888f","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:27:05.953Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I shouldn't hardcode the folder token. Let me think about this differently.\n\nActually, I realize there's a more fundamental issue. Looking at the `drive.media.uploadAll` API - it's used for uploading media to various document types. For `docx_image`, the `parent_node` is the document's node_token. For `bitable_image`, the `parent_node` should be the bitable's node_token.\n\nFor a bitable, the node in the folder hierarchy has a specific token. The `app_token` (like `BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f`) is the bitable's API identifier. The node_token for the same bitable might be different.\n \nThe node_token might follow a different format entirely. Rather than guessing, let me check what `xzq-xu/openclaw-plugin-feishu` does for bitable uploads, or pivot to uploading files via `drive.file.uploadAll` to cloud drive first, then using the `file_token` to create a proper download link in the bitable instead of an attachment.\n\nActually, looking back at the Feishu API docs for attachment fields, they expect a `file_token` that starts with `boxcn` from `drive.media.uploadAll`, not the `file_xxx` format from `drive.file.uploadAll`. But `drive.media.uploadAll` is returning a \"parent node not exist\" error, which makes me think the issue might be that bitable attachments actually require the newer v2 media upload API instead.","thinkingSignature":"1bf7a9da904d95b0f2e55dec782dc896a3ab6278ab25332d2d4bc5796aae3617"},{"type":"text","text":"等等，我想起来一个关键点——让我查一下飞书是否有 v2 版本的 media API：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_jxseubzob2of_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"media.*v2\\|v2.*media\\|uploadAllV2\\|upload_all\" /Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/feishu/node_modules/@larksuiteoapi/node-sdk/lib/index.js 2>/dev/null | head -10"}}],"api":"anth