{"type":"message","id":"6f2bec42","parentId":"5f0ea97b","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:27:43.222Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the SDK only has v1 of the media API. There's no v2.\n\nLet me take a completely fresh look at this problem.\n\nThe key error is \"parent node not exist.\" This means the `parent_node` value I'm passing doesn't correspond to an existing node in the Feishu drive.\n\nFor a bitable, there are multiple identifiers:\n1. `app_token` = `BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f` - for API calls\n2. `node_token` = the node in the drive hierarchy\n\nThese might be different values! When you create a bitable, it gets an `app_token` and also a `node_id` in the folder hierarchy. The `node_id` is what's needed for `parent_node`.\n \nWhen I look at the URL structure, the bitable has a `parent_token` in the folder hierarchy, but that's not the same as the `node_id` the API needs. The actual `node_id` for the bitable might be something like `bkn1xxxxxx`. I think I'm confusing what the API actually requires—the `parent_node` parameter should be the bitable's `node_id`, not the `app_token` I was trying to use.\n\nActually, looking back at the file.js documentation, it says for bitable types you should use the `app_token` as the `parent_node`. But when I tried that, I got \"parent node not exist.\" Maybe the bitable needs to be shared with the app first before it can be accessed as a parent node, similar to how the Feishu UI requires sharing a bitable to a bot. Or perhaps there's another scope or permission I'm missing.\n\nLet me step back and try the most direct approach: passing an empty string as `parent_node` for the bitable_image type, even though the docs say it's required. But wait—I already tested that and got the same \"parent node not exist\" error, so that clearly doesn't work. Maybe the issue isn't the `parent_node` itself but something about how the request is being formatted, like the boundary or content-type header. Or perhaps the bitable isn't actually mounted in the space or accessible to the user account making the API call.\n\nActually, I just realized—the bitable I created is in the user's personal space at the root level, not nested in a subfolder. That might be why the parent node lookup is failing. Let me try a completely different approach: upload the image to a Feishu doc instead, get the media token from that, then find a way to reference or embed that token in the bitable record.\n\nBut wait, there's another possibility I should check. When uploading to `docx_image`, the `parent_node` is the document ID and the `extra.drive_route_token` links it to the doc. For `bitable_image`, the `extra.bitablePerm.tableId` does something similar. What if `parent_node` for bitable should actually be a folder or wiki node instead of the bitable's app token? Maybe the bitable's app token works as a parent node for `drive.file.uploadAll`, but not for `drive.media.uploadAll`.\n\nLet me try uploading to the folder node instead and see if that resolves the issue.","thinkingSignature":"ac78b064eef288d8e4cf3f1bbeab2fab7c418ca6c4d0dc949a1434660a6ab80c"},{"type":"text","text":"等等，我发现一个重要线索——让我仔细看这个 bitable 的 `parent_token` 和节点关系：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_roud7ehyvz4o_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js","old_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    // 尝试用 folder token 作为 parent_node\n    const folderToken = 'nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, folder=${folderToken}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: folderToken,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });","new_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    // 尝试用 bitable 的 app_token 作为 parent_node\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: p.app_token,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n            extra: JSON.stringify({\n                bitablePerm: {\n                    tableId: p.table_id,\n                },\n            }),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":89996,"output":1150,"cacheRead":33389,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":124535,"cost":{"input":0.0269988,"output":0.00138,"cacheRead":0.0020033399999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03038214}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774510026192,"responseId":"061412cc2147fd22bc906f07aef8ae59"}}
{"type":"message","id":"d215ad2e","parentId":"6f2bec42","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:27:43.262Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_roud7ehyvz4o_1","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 377         });\n 378     }\n 379     const fileName = path.basename(filePath);\n 380     const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n-381     // 尝试用 folder token 作为 parent_node\n-382     const folderToken = 'nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf';\n-383     log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, folder=${folderToken}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n+381     // 尝试用 bitable 的 app_token 作为 parent_node\n+382     log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n 384     const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n 385         data: {\n 386             file_name: fileName,\n 387             parent_type: parentType,\n-388             parent_node: folderToken,\n+387             parent_node: p.app_token,\n 389             size: fileSize,\n 390             file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n+390             extra: JSON.stringify({\n+391                 bitablePerm: {\n+392                     tableId: p.table_id,\n+393                 },\n+394             }),\n 391         },\n 392     }, opts), { as: 'user' });\n 393     const fileToken = uploadRes?.file_token ?? uploadRes?.data?.file_token;\n 394     if (!fileToken) {\n     ...","firstChangedLine":381},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774510063254}}
{"type":"message","id":"a4ae3cc5","parentId":"d215ad2e","timestamp":"2026-03-26T07:28:08.658Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I reverted back to using `app_token` as `parent_node`. But that also gives \"parent node not exist.\" Let me think more carefully...\n\nActually, maybe the issue is that for `drive.media.uploadAll` with `bitable_image`, the `parent_node` needs to be the node_id of the bitable in the wiki/space hierarchy, not the `app_token`. For the official Feishu bitable, the `app_token` IS the node_id. But for some bitables, they might have separate node_id values.\n\nWait - I just realized something important. Looking at the drive file list again:\n- `🍎 苹果虾演示表` has `parent_token: \"nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf\"`\n\n\n- The bitable's own token is `BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f`\n\nWhen I tried the parent_node as the folder token, I still got \"parent node not exist.\" So maybe for `bitable_image` uploads, `parent_node` actually needs to be the bitable's node_id itself, which should be its token. But the app_token isn't working either. I'm wondering if the issue is that the bitable has to be in a specific space or location for the upload to work.\n\nLet me reconsider the error more carefully. \"parent node not exist\" could mean the node itself doesn't exist in the drive hierarchy, or the user doesn't have permission to access it. If the bitable was created directly in the user's personal space, the `app_token` might not actually map to a valid node_id in the drive API's context. For bitable specifically, the `app_token` and `node_id` might be completely separate identifiers. I should try passing the `parent_token` from the file list as the `parent_node` instead, since that represents the actual folder location in the hierarchy.","thinkingSignature":"081bdf3e69209920dbd42f18ffdf95508052bc07b3afa4d44643431092b36aeb"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bmxofblksrkc_1","name":"feishu_doc_media","arguments":{"action":"bitable_upload","app_token":"BeRBbpyd9a2eYusZbb1c7N4cn1f","table_id":"tbl3oA2By4N3FTPh","file_path":"/var/folders/8r/0b88l2d52ys5974p0fms08mr0000gn/T/demo_weather.png","type":"image","field_id":"fld9qWZcrV"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":89980,"output":553,"cacheRead":33389,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":123922,"cost":{"input":0.026993999999999997,"output":0.0006636,"cacheRead":0.0020033399999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.029660939999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774510063265,"responseId":"061412f3de30fc94e8c3034cfc4e2c88"}}
