{"type":"message","id":"70369458","parentId":"d5b144f9","timestamp":"2026-03-26T08:24:14.598Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Attachment field created with field_id \"fldAxrQj1V\". Now let me create a record first and then try to upload the image.Actually, let me think about this. The record creation doesn't need the image to be uploaded first - I can create a record with an empty attachment field, get the record_id, then upload the image using the record_id and field_id in the extra.But actually, looking at the Feishu docs again - the flow for uploading to a bitable attachment is:\n1. Upload the file to get a file_token using `drive.media.uploadAll` with `parent_type=bitable_image` and `parent_node=<app_token>`\n\n\n2. The returned file_token (format: boxcnxxx) is then used in the record creation/update\n\nI'm stuck on step 1 though - the parent_node validation is failing. Let me reconsider the documentation: the extra field with bitablePerm structure is only needed for advanced permissions, and for basic cases the parent_node should just be the app_token. But since my attempts are being rejected, maybe I need to provide the extra field even for regular uploads.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the core issue might be that the app_token alone isn't sufficient - the API-created bitable might not have a corresponding Drive entry, so there's nothing for parent_node to reference. Let me try a different approach and look for a dedicated bitable attachment upload API instead of relying on the generic media upload endpoint.","thinkingSignature":"1eeed8130505838310d9d8a9cb2180e0d859eb8e6d96bcb0dbc4f566f86186a8"},{"type":"text","text":"先创建一条记录，再试着往里加附件：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_exio4wpk0dlc_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"create","app_token":"UJZtbmw3Hav0zgs0RPzcvcrPnqe","table_id":"tblyQc7Iu7YRS7yV","fields":{"文本":"测试"}}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax