{"type":"message","id":"418f43d5","parentId":"7ddf14c5","timestamp":"2026-03-26T08:25:46.354Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the new bitable in the Drive list:- token: `UJZtbmw3Hav0zgs0RPzcvcrPnqe` \n- name: \"\" (empty - it's the \"未命名多维表格\")\n- parent_token: `nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf`\n- type: `bitable`So the new bitable DOES appear in Drive with the token `UJZtbmw3Hav0zgs0RPzcvcrPnqe` (which is the same as its app_token). \n\nThe bitable is located in the folder `nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf`. Now I'm realizing that when uploading a bitable image, the `parent_node` should actually be the bitable's app_token itself, and the table_id needs to be provided in the `extra` field—similar to how the docx_image upload works.\n\nFor bitable specifically, the flow seems to be uploading the image first to get a file_token, then using that token when creating or updating a record. The key question is what value `parent_node` should have when calling `drive.media.uploadAll` with `parent_type=bitable_image`. The docs mention it's a required field, and based on the Feishu UI, when you open a bitable and look at its URL structure, the app_token appears in the path—so maybe that's what belongs in `parent_node`.\n\nBut I've already tested this approach and it returned \"parent node not exist,\" which makes me wonder if the Drive service for bitable attachments uses a different token format than what I'm using. The example in the docs shows `bascni70rJDWTKvGNOmGHmabcef` as a sample value for bitable_image, suggesting there's a specific token format I'm missing. token. But that's just a placeholder example value! The actual token for a bitable would be the app_token like `UJZtbmw3Hav0zgs0RPzcvcrPnqe`. Looking at the error \"parent node not exist\" - the Drive service can't find a node with that token. This could mean the app_token isn't a valid Drive node for the media upload, or there's something else I'm missing about how the token maps to the actual Drive resource.\n\nLet me try using the folder token instead, or maybe I should just test with an empty string to see what happens. I'm also wondering if the bitable token might actually be a wiki token, or if there's a permissions issue with the user OAuth token - the error could be about read permission on the parent node rather than the node not existing at all. I've already tried the app_token and got the same \"parent node not exist\" error, so I need a different approach.\n\nLooking at the Feishu API documentation for bitable attachments, it seems the workflow is to first upload the file and get a file_token, then create or update the record with that token. But I'm realizing the issue might be that for bitable specifically, the `parent_node` might need to be something other than what I've been using - maybe an empty string could work since the extra field already specifies the bitablePerm tableId.\n\nActually, I just noticed something important: the `parent_type` values for bitable (`bascni...`) are different from what I've been trying. The Drive API for bitable might use a different token format than what I'm passing as the parent_node, so I need to figure out what the actual bitable node token is rather than using the app_token.","thinkingSignature":"d9e53f097ffa2b6caa0c6101516a7d290cec1daea122f0a8cce8b0ed89848904"},{"type":"text","text":"看到了！新 bitable 的 token 是 `UJZtbmw3Hav0zgs0RPzcvcrPnqe`，在 Drive 里显示 name 为空。\n\n让我试试用这个 bitable 的 token 作为 `parent_node`：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_3taxnlc0oy56_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-lark/src/tools/oapi/drive/doc-media.js","old_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    // extra 里放入 bitablePerm，包含 tableId 和 attachments 映射（record_id -> [file_token]）\n    // 先用一个占位 record_id，上传成功后会得到 file_token，再更新记录\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: p.table_id,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n            extra: JSON.stringify({\n                bitablePerm: {\n                    tableId: p.table_id,\n                },\n            }),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });","new_string":"    const parentType = mediaType === 'image' ? 'bitable_image' : 'bitable_file';\n    log.info(`bitable_upload: app=${p.app_token}, table=${p.table_id}, field=${p.field_id}, file=${fileName}, size=${fileSize}`);\n    // 对于 bitable_image/bitable_file，parent_node 应为 bitable 在 Drive 里的 token（即 app_token）\n    const uploadRes = await client.invoke('feishu_doc_media.bitable_upload', (sdk, opts) => sdk.drive.v1.media.uploadAll({\n        data: {\n            file_name: fileName,\n            parent_type: parentType,\n            parent_node: p.app_token,\n            size: fileSize,\n            file: (0, node_fs_1.createReadStream)(filePath),\n            extra: JSON.stringify({\n                bitablePerm: {\n                    tableId: p.table_id,\n                },\n            }),\n        },\n    }, opts), { as: 'user' });"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":86506,"output":1282,"cacheRead":33389,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121177,"cost":{"input":0.025951799999999997,"output":0.0015383999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0020033399999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.029493539999999995}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774513502643,"responseId":"06142062799d7e4f7f78a3ceb5384d72"}}
