{"type":"message","id":"016c46c3","parentId":"173570d4","timestamp":"2026-03-26T09:37:47.602Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if it's done. I've been stuck on the \"parent node not exist\" error. Let me be honest about the situation and think about what to do next.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole problem. I've been going in circles trying different parent_node values. Let me think about this more carefully.\n\nThe key issue is: `drive.media.uploadAll` with `parent_type='bitable_image'` requires a valid `parent_node`. All attempts with various tokens fail.\n\nWait - I just realized something. The folder token `nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf` was shown in the drive file list as the parent of the bitable files. \n\nWhen I tried `drive.media.uploadAll` with `parent_node='nodcnKUq3QN9lNcCRr9WtG8pjvf'` and `parent_type='bitable_image'`, it failed with \"parent node not exist.\" This suggests the issue might be that a folder token can't serve as a parent for bitable media uploads - the parent_node needs to be a bitable-specific token, not just any folder.\n\nI'm also wondering if the real problem is that these bitables were created through the API rather than through the Feishu UI, which might mean they don't have the internal node structure needed for the media upload API to recognize them as valid parents.\n\nBut I should consider an alternative approach entirely: instead of using the bitable media upload API, what if I create the record first and then directly update it with the attachment field using the standard record update API? That way I could potentially bypass the parent_node issue altogether.","thinkingSignature":"81032231572c45413898cca709e4bf5265906bdd79c26edabd2bc8f0fd1593be"},{"type":"text","text":"还没好，还在卡着 😅\n\n`bitable_image` 的 `parent_node` 问题一直解决不了，试了各种 token 都不行。\n\n**换个方向——不折腾上传了，直接用记录更新 API 写入附件字段：**\n\n图片上传到云盘后有 token，虽然不是 bitable 专用格式，但我试试直接把这个 token 写入记录的附件字段，看飞书能不能接受：\n"},{"type":"