{"type":"message","id":"508e70a8","parentId":"146e42c6","timestamp":"2026-03-26T09:47:11.948Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The search results show an interesting result: \"粉丝定制的'企业级'工作流！飞书多维表格控制RunningHub，填表即出图并自动回传，全自动闭环\" and a video \"如何通过飞书API讲图片上传至飞书多维表格\". These seem relevant! Let me also note the Bilibili video URL: `https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1UC4y1C7Zi/`\n\nAlso interestingly, there's a mention of \"ArkClaw | AI智能体\" and \"别手动填表了！用 OpenClaw'养龙虾'\" - this is about OpenClaw being used with Feishu for automation!\n \nBut the most relevant reference is that Zhihu article from earlier - it actually demonstrates uploading images to Feishu bitable via API with working code. Let me try accessing it again. The Python example shows the critical part: it passes `parent_type='bitable_image'` and `parent_node=table_apptoken` to the upload endpoint, which suggests the real issue might be that the table's app_token isn't being formatted correctly or passed in the right way.\n\nI'm wondering if using `user_access_token` versus `tenant_access_token` could be the differentiator here, since the OpenClaw plugin might be using the token type differently than the working example does.","thinkingSignature":"a740126bc4fe5d1a5d3bbb19716ec973ea1c56da3324acc8277f77f920c8fe17"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_la4idatyjdpb_1","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"feishu bitable attachment field upload python requests library parent_node table_apptoken example code"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":85173,"output":324,"cacheRead":33639,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":119136,"cost":{"input":0.0255519,"output":0.00038879999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00201834,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02795904}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774518417155,"responseId":"0614339401bdd921378f10568945bb57"}}
