{"type":"message","id":"5dbbfa42","parentId":"f8ec7e77","timestamp":"2026-03-26T09:48:00.126Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me look at the openclaw.json to find the Feishu app credentials. I shouldn't expose these though - let me think about how to use them responsibly.\n\nActually, the user is the owner of this system and the app is their own app. It should be fine to use the credentials to test the API directly.\n\nBut wait - I should not extract and display the actual app_id and app_secret in my response for security reasons. Let me use a script to get the token and make the API call internally.\n\nLet me write a Node.js script that:\n1. Gets the app_access_token using the SDK's auth method\n2. Makes a direct curl call to the drive media upload API to test the bitable_image parent_node\n\nActually, I should be more careful here. The app credentials are in openclaw.json and I shouldn't expose them. Let me just read the necessary values internally without displaying them.","thinkingSignature":"b8ccc93ac2fed4d445405c59b1c07034177c0e14d8feebc81e2fc0a34360807c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1syrf3u6flin_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 读取飞书 app 凭证\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/Users/edy/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f:\n    config = json.load(f)\nfeishu = config.get('channels', {}).get('feishu', {})\nprint('app_id:', feishu.get('appId', 'not found'))\nprint('app_secret:', '****' if feishu.get('appSecret') else 'not found')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":87427,"output":306,"cacheRead":33639,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121372,"cost":{"input":0.026228099999999997,"output":0.0003672,"cacheRead":0.00201834,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02861364}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774518461459,"responseId":"061433c05e9f44ea1217a845cd555b27"}}
