{"type":"message","id":"6075ec26","parentId":"11e87f61","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:13:48.103Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"让我看看 mac/skills.md 文档。","thinkingSignature":"7c504ef767077f75969b71bb0f974ee88737c361876243413ade0816264e1b3c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_i43fuzcldyr0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/platforms/mac/skills.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":87605,"output":51,"cacheRead":33639,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121295,"cost":{"input":0.0262815,"output":0.0000612,"cacheRead":0.00201834,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02836104}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774534425112,"responseId":"06147219f6c39d9e68f8d95373356ad9"}}
{"type":"message","id":"b07a0074","parentId":"6075ec26","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:13:48.145Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_i43fuzcldyr0_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"macOS Skills settings UI and gateway-backed status\"\nread_when:\n  - Updating the macOS Skills settings UI\n  - Changing skills gating or install behavior\ntitle: \"Skills (macOS)\"\n---\n\n# Skills (macOS)\n\nThe macOS app surfaces OpenClaw skills via the gateway; it does not parse skills locally.\n\n## Data source\n\n- `skills.status` (gateway) returns all skills plus eligibility and missing requirements\n  (including allowlist blocks for bundled skills).\n- Requirements are derived from `metadata.openclaw.requires` in each `SKILL.md`.\n\n## Install actions\n\n- `metadata.openclaw.install` defines install options (brew/node/go/uv).\n- The app calls `skills.install` to run installers on the gateway host.\n- The gateway surfaces only one preferred installer when multiple are provided\n  (brew when available, otherwise node manager from `skills.install`, default npm).\n\n## Env/API keys\n\n- The app stores keys in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` under `skills.entries.<skillKey>`.\n- `skills.update` patches `enabled`, `apiKey`, and `env`.\n\n## Remote mode\n\n- Install + config updates happen on the gateway host (not the local Mac)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":10,"aggregated":"---\nsummary: \"macOS Skills settings UI and gateway-backed status\"\nread_when:\n  - Updating the macOS Skills settings UI\n  - Changing skills gating or install behavior\ntitle: \"Skills (macOS)\"\n---\n\n# Skills (macOS)\n\nThe macOS app surfaces OpenClaw skills via the gateway; it does not parse skills locally.\n\n## Data source\n\n- `skills.status` (gateway) returns all skills plus eligibility and missing requirements\n  (including allowlist blocks for bundled skills).\n- Requirements are derived from `metadata.openclaw.requires` in each `SKILL.md`.\n\n## Install actions\n\n- `metadata.openclaw.install` defines install options (brew/node/go/uv).\n- The app calls `skills.install` to run installers on the gateway host.\n- The gateway surfaces only one preferred installer when multiple are provided\n  (brew when available, otherwise node manager from `skills.install`, default npm).\n\n## Env/API keys\n\n- The app stores keys in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` under `skills.entries.<skillKey>`.\n- `skills.update` patches `enabled`, `apiKey`, and `env`.\n\n## Remote mode\n\n- Install + config updates happen on the gateway host (not the local Mac).","cwd":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774534428139}}
{"type":"message","id":"d92ac396","parentId":"b07a0074","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:13:51.995Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"这个文档说的是 macOS App 的 Skills UI，跟命令行 skills 工具不一样。让我看看 clawhub.md 文档，了解一下如何安装本地 skill。","thinkingSignature":"238dc8d2e1e9eceec95eae8800fe8b41a1ec04de13ebeb1411d15ea551eb444e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_965qkdyuxa4x_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md | head -80"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":87924,"output":74,"cacheRead":33639,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121637,"cost":{"input":0.0263772,"output":0.00008879999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00201834,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02848434}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774534428147,"responseId":"0614721cde2cc3297917700846b305ca"}}
{"type":"message","id":"d6924a76","parentId":"d92ac396","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:13:52.040Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_965qkdyuxa4x_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"ClawHub guide: public registry, native OpenClaw install flows, and ClawHub CLI workflows\"\nread_when:\n  - Introducing ClawHub to new users\n  - Installing, searching, or publishing skills\n  - Explaining ClawHub CLI flags and sync behavior\ntitle: \"ClawHub\"\n---\n\n# ClawHub\n\nClawHub is the public registry for **OpenClaw skills and plugins**.\n\n- Use native `openclaw` commands to search/install/update skills and install\n  plugins from ClawHub.\n- Use the separate `clawhub` CLI when you need registry auth, publish, delete,\n  undelete, or sync workflows.\n\nSite: [clawhub.ai](https://clawhub.ai)\n\n## Native OpenClaw flows\n\nSkills:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw skills search \"calendar\"\nopenclaw skills install <skill-slug>\nopenclaw skills update --all\n```\n\nPlugins:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install clawhub:<package>\nopenclaw plugins update --all\n```\n\nBare npm-safe plugin specs are also tried against ClawHub before npm:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install openclaw-codex-app-server\n```\n\nNative `openclaw` commands install into your active workspace and persist source\nmetadata so later `update` calls can stay on ClawHub.\n\n## What ClawHub is\n\n- A public registry for OpenClaw skills.\n- A versioned store of skill bundles and metadata.\n- A discovery surface for search, tags, and usage signals.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. A user publishes a skill bundle (files + metadata).\n2. ClawHub stores the bundle, parses metadata, and assigns a version.\n3. The registry indexes the skill for search and discovery.\n4. Users browse, download, and install skills in OpenClaw.\n\n## What you can do\n\n- Publish new skills and new versions of existing skills.\n- Discover skills by name, tags, or search.\n- Download skill bundles and inspect their files.\n- Report skills that are abusive or unsafe.\n- If you are a moderator, hide, unhide, delete, or ban.\n\n## Who this is for (beginner-friendly)\n\nIf you want to add new capabilities to your OpenClaw agent, ClawHub is the easiest way to find and install skills. You do not need to know how the backend works. You can:\n\n- Search for skills by plain language.\n- Install a skill into your workspace.\n- Update skills later with one command.\n- Back up your own skills by publishing them.\n\n## Quick start (non-technical)\n\n1. Search for something you need:\n   - `openclaw skills search \"calendar\"`"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":11,"aggregated":"---\nsummary: \"ClawHub guide: public registry, native OpenClaw install flows, and ClawHub CLI workflows\"\nread_when:\n  - Introducing ClawHub to new users\n  - Installing, searching, or publishing skills\n  - Explaining ClawHub CLI flags and sync behavior\ntitle: \"ClawHub\"\n---\n\n# ClawHub\n\nClawHub is the public registry for **OpenClaw skills and plugins**.\n\n- Use native `openclaw` commands to search/install/update skills and install\n  plugins from ClawHub.\n- Use the separate `clawhub` CLI when you need registry auth, publish, delete,\n  undelete, or sync workflows.\n\nSite: [clawhub.ai](https://clawhub.ai)\n\n## Native OpenClaw flows\n\nSkills:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw skills search \"calendar\"\nopenclaw skills install <skill-slug>\nopenclaw skills update --all\n```\n\nPlugins:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install clawhub:<package>\nopenclaw plugins update --all\n```\n\nBare npm-safe plugin specs are also tried against ClawHub before npm:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install openclaw-codex-app-server\n```\n\nNative `openclaw` commands install into your active workspace and persist source\nmetadata so later `update` calls can stay on ClawHub.\n\n## What ClawHub is\n\n- A public registry for OpenClaw skills.\n- A versioned store of skill bundles and metadata.\n- A discovery surface for search, tags, and usage signals.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. A user publishes a skill bundle (files + metadata).\n2. ClawHub stores the bundle, parses metadata, and assigns a version.\n3. The registry indexes the skill for search and discovery.\n4. Users browse, download, and install skills in OpenClaw.\n\n## What you can do\n\n- Publish new skills and new versions of existing skills.\n- Discover skills by name, tags, or search.\n- Download skill bundles and inspect their files.\n- Report skills that are abusive or unsafe.\n- If you are a moderator, hide, unhide, delete, or ban.\n\n## Who this is for (beginner-friendly)\n\nIf you want to add new capabilities to your OpenClaw agent, ClawHub is the easiest way to find and install skills. You do not need to know how the backend works. You can:\n\n- Search for skills by plain language.\n- Install a skill into your workspace.\n- Update skills later with one command.\n- Back up your own skills by publishing them.\n\n## Quick start (non-technical)\n\n1. Search for something you need:\n   - `openclaw skills search \"calendar\"`","cwd":"/Users/edy/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774534432034}}
{"type":"message","id":"2653fb33","parentId":"d6924a76","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:14:09.100Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"原来 `openclaw skills install` 只能从 ClawHub 安装。让我看看文档后面有没有说怎么从本地文件安装。根据文档：\n- `openclaw skills install <skill-slug>` - 从 ClawHub 安装\n- 没有看到从本地 .skill 文件安装的命令\n\n但是之前 `package_skill.py` 把它打包成了 .skill 文件。也许我需要用 `clawhub` CLI 来安装本地 skill。让我试试 `clawhub` 命令行工具。\n\n或者，也许更简单的方法是：直接把 skill 文件放到正确的位置，让 OpenClaw 自动发现。\n\n根据 Skills 的工作原理：\n- 文档说 \"Skills provide specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools\" \n\n\n- 它们被打包成 .skill 文件分发\n\n`.skill` 文件实际上是一个 zip 文件，里面包含 SKILL.md 和资源文件夹。也许我应该用 `clawhub` CLI 来安装这个本地的 .skill 文件。","thinkingSignature":"7c433fc248b79eb2a4051cc95d271826f2098f1d962dfe8837494be2a1aba6d3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xvyhzboonuft_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"which clawhub 2>/dev/null && clawhub --help 2>&1 | head -20 || echo \"clawhub not found\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":86508,"output":236,"cacheRead":33639,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":120383,"cost":{"input":0.0259524,"output":0.0002832,"cacheRead":0.00201834,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02825394}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774534432042,"responseId":"06147220287710b40021ad302c929a39"}}
